    counts the preview slots as well: README's five and docs/gui.md's one, each
    filled by a marker naming the right file or by an upload to GitHub's CDN,
    the two counts adding up, and a relative .mp4 image link refused as the
    dead shape it is.  That is what lets the upload commit stay green - the
    markers exist to be deleted - while still seeing a hole where one was.
    Pointedly no byte hash, because x264 output is its version's business.  It
    also drives the tool for all five themes through the animated path at 160 px
    (the themes take different render options, and passing one option bag
    straight through died with `theme_alpha() got an unexpected keyword argument
    'source'`), writes one pinned GIF to keep the caption shape honest (#ffc400
    lands as (252, 197, 2), 3/255 off), and samples two live readings to prove
